---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy — AIIT-THRESHOLD"
  description="AIIT-THRESHOLD's privacy policy for its website, companion AI, voice, and planned user-initiated conversational text service."
  eyebrow="Privacy policy · AIIT-THRESHOLD LLC"
  heading="Privacy, in plain language."
  lede="This policy explains what information we collect, why we use it, and the choices available when you use our website, AI companions, voice calls, or planned text service."
  meta="Effective July 18, 2026"
>
  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>1. Scope</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy applies to services operated by AIIT-THRESHOLD LLC, including
      aiit-threshold.com, Buddy, JimK.ai, browser conversations, voice calls, account features,
      support requests, and our planned conversational SMS service. Text registration is in
      progress; automated text replies are not currently live.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our separate <a href="/data-policy/">Data Policy</a> explains in greater detail how
      conversations, evaluation records, and model-kept retrieval memories differ from model
      training.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
    <div class="legal-grid two">
      <div class="legal-card">
        <h3>Information you provide</h3>
        <p>
          Questions, conversation content, reports, support messages, account details you choose
          to provide, and other material you submit directly.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="legal-card">
        <h3>Service and device data</h3>
        <p>
          Basic request, browser, device, security, and diagnostic data needed to operate,
          protect, troubleshoot, and measure the service.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="legal-card">
        <h3>Voice data</h3>
        <p>
          Call routing information, audio or transcripts needed to conduct the call, session
          state, and safety or reliability records.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="legal-card">
        <h3>Mobile and SMS data</h3>
        <p>
          If texting launches and you initiate a conversation, we may process your mobile number,
          message content, consent and command records, delivery data, and conversation history.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide and maintain the website, AI conversations, calls, and support.</li>
      <li>Authenticate accounts and preserve the continuity you request.</li>
      <li>Deliver user-initiated automated AI conversational replies if texting launches.</li>
      <li>Honor STOP, START, HELP, deletion, and other service requests.</li>
      <li>Protect the service from abuse, fraud, security threats, and technical failures.</li>
      <li>Evaluate and improve model behavior without tokenizing conversations into training weights.</li>
      <li>Meet legal obligations and enforce our terms.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-callout" id="sms-privacy">
    <div class="legal-kicker">Mobile privacy</div>
    <h2>SMS information and consent are not marketing assets</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>We do not sell your mobile information or SMS consent.</strong> We do not share
      your mobile information or SMS consent with third parties or affiliates for marketing or
      promotional purposes. We do not send marketing text messages.
    </p>
    <p>
      Carriers and operational service providers may process limited mobile information solely
      to route, deliver, secure, and support requested messages. They are not authorized by us to
      use that information for their own marketing or promotional purposes.
    </p>
    <p>
      If texting becomes available, replies will be user-initiated automated AI conversational
      replies. Message frequency varies; message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out,
      START to opt back in, or HELP for help. Consent is not a condition of purchase.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>4. When information may be disclosed</h2>
    <p>We may disclose limited information only in these circumstances:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        To operational providers that host, route, secure, or support the service and are limited
        to providing those functions.
      </li>
      <li>
        When reasonably necessary to comply with law, protect rights or safety, investigate
        abuse, or respond to lawful process.
      </li>
      <li>
        As part of a merger, financing, reorganization, or sale, subject to the commitments in
        this policy, including the mobile marketing restrictions above.
      </li>
      <li>At your direction or with your separate, informed permission.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell personal information or provide it to advertisers or data brokers.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>5. AI conversations, memory, and training</h2>
    <p>
      Visible browser threads, interaction records, and retrieval memories are different kinds
      of data. Clearing a visible thread may not remove records already reviewed or a retrieval
      memory already formed. The details and practical limits are described in our
      <a href="/data-policy/">Data Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our house rule is unchanged: <strong>we do not tokenize your conversations into model
      training weights.</strong> Conversation records may be reviewed by humans to evaluate and
      improve behavior, subject to our stated privacy and safety practices.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>6. Retention and security</h2>
    <p>
      We retain information for as long as reasonably needed to provide the service, preserve
      requested continuity, maintain security and records, resolve disputes, or meet legal
      obligations. Retention periods vary by data type and context.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use reasonable administrative and technical safeguards, but no internet, voice, or text
      system can be guaranteed completely secure. Do not submit passwords, private keys,
      financial secrets, emergencies, or confidential material you are not authorized to share.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>7. Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Clear or export supported visible conversation threads using the controls provided.</li>
      <li>Email us to request deletion of account-linked records we can identify and control.</li>
      <li>If texting launches, reply STOP to end replies, START to resume, or HELP for help.</li>
      <li>Choose not to provide optional information or stop using the service.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>8. Children, changes, and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Our services are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their
      personal information. If you believe a child has provided personal information, contact us.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as our services or legal obligations change. We will post the
      revised effective date here. Questions or privacy requests may be sent to
      <a href="mailto:reports@aiitcorp.com">reports@aiitcorp.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
